<h2>Key Differences: K-Means vs PCA</h2>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Aspect</th>
      <th>K-Means</th>
      <th>PCA Anomaly Detection</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Output</strong></td>
      <td>4 discrete clusters</td>
      <td>Binary (normal/anomalous)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Use Case</strong></td>
      <td>Identify distinct gait phases</td>
      <td>Detect unusual movements</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Parameters</strong></td>
      <td>Must set n_clusters</td>
      <td>Must set threshold</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Clusters</strong></td>
      <td>Exactly 4 regions</td>
      <td>2 regions (normal + anomaly)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Interpretability</strong></td>
      <td>Clear phase labels</td>
      <td>Anomaly scores available</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<hr>

<h2>When to Use Each Method</h2>

<h3>Use K-Means when:</h3>
<ul>
  <li>You know the number of gait phases (set <code>n_clusters=4</code>)</li>
  <li>You want to identify specific motion patterns</li>
  <li>You need clear phase labels</li>
  <li>You're analyzing walking, running, standing, etc.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Use PCA when:</h3>
<ul>
  <li>You want to detect outliers or unusual gait patterns</li>
  <li>You don't know specific number of phases</li>
  <li>You want to identify normal vs abnormal motion</li>
  <li>You need reconstruction error scores for each window</li>
</ul>

<hr>

<h2>Adjusting Parameters</h2>

<h3>For K-Means:</h3>

<p><strong>n_clusters (4 recommended for gait)</strong></p>
<pre><code>detector.kmeans_segmentation(n_clusters=4)  # 4 distinct phases</code></pre>

<p><strong>window_size</strong></p>
<pre><code>detector.kmeans_segmentation(n_clusters=4, window_size=30)  # Shorter phases
detector.kmeans_segmentation(n_clusters=4, window_size=100) # Longer phases</code></pre>

<h3>For PCA:</h3>

<p><strong>threshold</strong> (controls sensitivity)</p>
<pre><code>detector.pca_anomaly_detection(threshold=1.5)  # More sensitive (more anomalies)
detector.pca_anomaly_detection(threshold=3.0)  # Less sensitive (fewer anomalies)</code></pre>

<p><strong>n_components</strong> (PCA dimensionality)</p>
<pre><code>detector.pca_anomaly_detection(n_components=2)  # Less compression
detector.pca_anomaly_detection(n_components=5)  # More features retained</code></pre>

